ical Syriac ܣܩܪܩܐ (sqrqˀ), ܣܝܩܘܪܩܐ (syqwrqˀ /⁠sīqūrqā⁠/), Arabic سُكُرُّجَة (sukurruja), Proto-Slavic *skovorda and Old Armenian սկաւառակ (skawaṙak), the latter probably from earlier *սկաւար(ի)րակ (*skawar(i)rak), from Iranian *skavarid-ak containing the well-know"},{"parola":"سیکی","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"bottle gourd, calabash","termine_origine":"σικύα","catena":[{"codice":"grc","nome":"Ancient Greek","termine":"σικύα","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"grc","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Ancient Greek σικύα (sikúa)."},{"parola":"فانوس","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"lantern","termine_origine":"φανός","catena":[{"codice":"grc","nome":"Ancient Greek","termine":"φανός","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"grc","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Ultimately from Ancient Greek φανός (phanós, “lantern”)."},{"parola":"فرچی","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"Probably","significato":"cloak","termine_origine":"φᾶρος","catena":[{"codice":"grc","nome":"Ancient Greek","termine":"φᾶρος","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"grc","ambiti":["moda"],"via":"","testo":"Probably from Ancient Greek φᾶρος (phâros)."},{"parola":"فشنگ","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"Possibly","significato":"cartridge (firearms package)","termine_origine":"φυσίγγη","catena":[{"codice":"grc","nome":"Ancient Greek","termine":"φυσίγγη","categoria":"prestito"}],"lontana":"grc","ambiti":["militare"],"via":"ar","testo":"* From فش (feš, “(archaic) a sibilant or hissing sound”). * According to Dehkhoda, possibly from گلفهشنگ (galafahšang, golfahšang, “stalagmite”). * According to Mo'in Dictionary, via Arabic, supposedly from پشنگ (pašang, “splash”) * A common narrative in the West derives from Ancient Greek φυσίγγη ("},{"parola":"فلنج","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"catego